E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:8:9-18 struct-marker "word struct `TwoFields` fields total 128 bits, and a word holds 64" #"refused here" !"a word struct is one machine word, not a block (docs/memory-model.md MM-VAL-10a)" ?"drop a field or narrow one until the widths fit in 64 bits"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:13:8-9 struct-marker "field `x` of word struct `Mutable` is `mut`" #"refused here" !"a word struct has no block a field store could reach" ?"drop `mut`: a word struct is a value, and a store would change only the copy it was made on"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:16:4-5 struct-marker "field `x` of word struct `NotAWord` is not a fixed-width field" #"refused here" !"a `String`, a `Vec` or a record is a reference, and a word that held one would take no share of it" ?"type it `Int8`, `Int16`, `Int32`, `Int64`, `UInt8`, `UInt16`, `UInt32`, `UInt64`, or a `Link` of width `UInt8`, `UInt16` or `UInt32`. One `Int` field is the whole word"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:18:9-15 struct-marker "word struct `Params` takes type parameters" #"refused here" !"a word takes no share and so has no evidence a type argument could describe" ?"drop the parameters: a word carries no type argument"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:21:9-19 struct-marker "struct `SharedHeap` is `shared` but neither a `word` nor `sealed`" #"refused here" !"a `sealed shared` struct is lent to a `parallel` form's bindings with its count frozen until the last join, since `axiom_retain` is a plain load-add-store (MM-PAR-6b, MM-PAR-16)" ?"add `word` for a one-word handle or `sealed` for a counted one, or drop `shared`: only a module that keeps the fields to itself can promise every operation is safe from several bindings at once"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:24:20-24 struct-marker "`word` is written twice" #"refused here" !"a marker says one thing about the struct, and saying it twice says nothing more" ?"write each marker once"
E AX3084 1065-struct-marker.ax:27:17-23 struct-marker "`packed` is not a struct marker" #"refused here" !"the markers come between the name and the first field: `(struct Ticket word shared (slot : Int))`" ?"a struct takes `word`, which makes it one machine word rather than a heap block, `sealed`, which keeps its constructor and fields in its module, and `shared`, which lets a `parallel` binding capture it; anything else after the struct's name is refused"
